    }
   },
   {
    "id": "manohara-en-s025-u006",
    "kind": "dialogue",
    "speakerLabel": "வச",
    "text": "Hmm... hesitation has been born... poor you! What can you do? The people of the assembly will not permit it. So what if you are emperor—you must still fear ordinary subjects, must you not!",
    "source": {
     "sourcePath": "works/manohara/dialogues/records/scene-025.json",
     "canonicalScenePath": "works/manohara/scenes/scene-025.md",
     "sourceRecordId": "manohara-s025-d005",
     "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
     "sourceLocator": null,
     "pageProvenance": [
      {
       "pdf_page": 37,
       "printed_page": 36
      }
     ]
    },
    "translation": {
     "mode": "prose-faithful",
     "notes": [
      "Vasantha Sena's insinuating progression from hesitation to the emperor's fear of ordinary subjects is preserved."
     ]
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "manohara-en-s025-u007",
    "kind": "dialogue",
    "speakerLabel": "அர",
    "text": "No... you may come......",
    "source": {
     "sourcePath": "works/manohara/dialogues/records/scene-025.json",
     "canonicalScenePath": "works/manohara/scenes/scene-025.md",
     "sourceRecordId": "manohara-s025-d006",
     "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
     "sourceLocator": null,
     "pageProvenance": [
      {
       "pdf_page": 37,
       "printed_page": 36
      }
     ]
    },
    "translation": {
     "mode": "prose-faithful"
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "manohara-en-s025-u008",
    "kind": "dialogue",
    "speakerLabel": "வச",
    "text": "I may come!... What does it matter where I come? On that Ratna throne brought from the enemy land, can this wretched woman—who day and night performs penance thinking only of your love—sit beside you like the chief queen? Am I a sinner blessed with such fortune?",
    "source": {
     "sourcePath": "works/manohara/dialogues/records/scene-025.json",
     "canonicalScenePath": "works/manohara/scenes/scene-025.md",
     "sourceRecordId": "manohara-s025-d007",
     "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
     "sourceLocator": null,
     "pageProvenance": [
      {
       "pdf_page": 37,
       "printed_page": 36
      }
     ]
    },
    "translation": {
     "mode": "prose-faithful",
     "notes": [
      "The self-abasing `தரித்திரம் பிடித்தவள்` and ironic `கொடுத்து வைத்த பாவி` are retained rather than neutralized."
     ]
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "manohara-en-s025-u009",
    "kind": "dialogue",
    "speakerLabel": "அர",
    "text": "Why merely beside me—if I had strength like Paramasiva, I would keep you even upon my head, like the Ganga!",
    "source": {
     "sourcePath": "works/manohara/dialogues/records/scene-025.json",
     "canonicalScenePath": "works/manohara/scenes/scene-025.md",
     "sourceRecordId": "manohara-s025-d008",
     "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
     "sourceLocator": null,
     "pageProvenance": [
